1.1.38 (4/03/2020)
- 5 second debounce on network status changes

1.1.37 (2/04/2020)
- Support RAAT__VOLUME_TYPE_HIDDEN_NUMBER for devices that have a volume number that is not user facing

1.1.36 (4/02/2019)
- ALSA output plugin: failures to set channel map are no longer considered fatal, to accommodate USB devices that don't support channel mapping

1.1.35 (3/18/2019)
- Remove subnet scanning from discovery protocol

1.1.34 (2/25/2019)
- Fixed a race condition in the blocking stream read implementation
- Fixed a situation where an interrupted discovery cycle could cause a hang while shutting down a RAAT__Device
- Fixed a small memory leak around connection management

1.1.33 (11/30/2018)
-  ALSA output plugin: 100ms sleep on format changes to work around XMOS USB chipset bug

1.1.32 (09/02/2018)
-  ALSA output plugin: support MQA conditionals for sync_offset_ns

1.1.31 (07/09/2018)
-  Make RC__now_us and RC__now_ns use the same clock reference. This prevents network timeouts when the system clock changes

1.1.30 (05/18/2018)
- ALSA Volume Plugin: use correct mute element 

1.1.29 (03/22/2018)
- Support toggle_mute in incremental volume mode

1.1.28 (02/01/2018)
- Remove MQA related test code in ALSA plugin

1.1.27 (01/11/2018)
- Fix a regression introduced in 1.1.24 that caused "set_mute" to crash.

1.1.25 (01/11/2018)
- Add support for devices that require runtime format support probing (currently this is just for iOS)
- Add documentation for supporting MQA + Tilt controls in Signal Path to raat_docs.h
- Merge changes from Roon 1.4 mainline
- Fix audio artifacts that happened in conjunction with CoreAudio SRC on Macs

1.1.24 (01/11/2018)
- Add support for incremental (+/- buttons only) volume controls

1.1.23 (09/19/2017)
- Fix use of incorrect callback function while handling a crash within a RAAT client session

1.1.22 (09/19/2017)
- Use RL/RR instead of LLC/RLC for 5,6,7ch mappings. Only impacts multichannel devices

1.1.21 (07/06/2017)
- Fix a crash when output plugins exhibit unusual callback timing
- Fix a race condition that can result in "hung" or partially responsive connections

1.1.20 (06/28/2017)
- Support for MQA information in RAAT__StreamFormat so that devices can know when they are about to receive an MQA stream

1.1.19 (04/26/2017)
- Added a "noalloc" option for reading TCP streams using luv
- Disable FS access in luv/lua
- Miscellaneous bug fixes related to CoreAudio/WASAPI
- Support for DSD512/768k in non-ALSA backends

1.1.18 (04/04/2017)
- Fix a situation where stale data can be used in zone grouping slave situations

1.1.17 (03/17/2017)
- Fix a discovery-related crash when processing multiple network status updates in rapid succession

1.1.16 (03/09/2017)
- Fix a situation where stale data can be used in zone grouping slave situations

1.1.15 (02/15/2017)
- Fix RAAT__device_stop hanging in network interface watching code

1.1.14 (01/19/2017)
- Improvements to drift correction algorithm to make situations with larger clock rate differences tractable
- Added an option for the "null" output that allows it to emulate arbitrary clock rates for testing of drift correction
- Added an 'exit' command to raatool to help with testing crash/restart behavior
- Bugfixes for WASAPI, CoreAudio, ASIO output plugins and WASAPI volume plugin (merged from Roon 1.3 development)

1.1.13 (01/12/2017)
- Support for tracking the types of connected clients

1.1.12 (01/02/2017)
- Performance optimizations geared towards reducing heap activity during audio streaming

1.1.11 (12/16/2016)
- Improved management of discovery behavior when network interfaces go up and down on Linux

1.1.10 (11/16/2016)
- RAAT__stream supports channel mapping so that multi-channel playback can be efficient even when sending blank channels
- Stop inadvertently setting the device format durring non-exclusive-mode CoreAudio (Mac) playback
- Fix rapid-fire volume/mute commands for WASAPI (windows) volume plugin, since they confuse some drivers
- Fix deadlock + crash in ASIO (windows) output plugin
- Fix a bug that prevented DSD_MODE_NONE from working properly under some circumstances in the WASAPI (windows) output plugin 

1.1.9 (10/21/2016)
- Add support for auto_name in info dict

1.1.8 (9/30/2016)
- Sweep for memory leaks
- ALSA Output plugin adds support for special situations where ALSA devices aren't around at RAAT startup (not for external USB devices)

