- Fix regression in recent RAAT__Stream fix

1.1.6 (9/8/2016)
- Fix regression in recent RAAT__Stream optimizations 

1.1.5 (9/1/2016)
- Fix ALSA buffer size computation

1.1.4 (8/23/2016)
- Memory pooling in RAAT__Stream to reduce malloc heap usage
- Optimized luv's UDP receiver to avoid address parsing/conversion overhead
- Optimized luv's UDP receiver to avoid creating unneeded options dictionaries
- Added moving average to drift correction algorithm to smooth out poor network connections

1.1.3 (8/22/2016)
- Optimized duplicate packet detection in raat_stream.c

1.1.2 (7/28/2016)
- Fixed a memory leak in raat_discovery.c

1.1.1 (6/24/2016)
- Fixed two memory leaks in raat_session.c

1.1.0 (6/1/2016)
- Backported all RAAT changes that were made for Roon's 1.2 release into the SDK
- Fixed an error in the sample stuff/drop implementation that could cause audible artifacts during drift compensation corrections
- ALSA output: for devices that only support >2 channel output, zero-fill the remaining channels
- Support get_output_delay on outputs to avoid clipping content at stream start on devices with unusually long delays
- ALSA output: Add some extra retries to work around issues with certain USB devices.
- ALSA output: report PCM support up to 1411200hz and DSD support up to DSD1024 if the ALSA device supports it. 
- ALSA output: support for up to 10 output channels
- ALSA output: prefers larger DSD sample formats to smaller ones
- Resource management should be significantly more robust if destroying and re-creating RAAT__Device instances without resarting the process.
- ALSA volume plugin is somewhat better about choosing the correct volume control for pcm512x devices
- A lot of code was moved from raat into rcore with some light API renames to faciliate reuse in other areas
- Many other small bug fixes and stability improvements throughout the core RAAT infrastructure
- More audio output plugin implementations (CoreAudio, ASIO, WASAPI) are available. 
- More volume plugin implementations (CoreAudio, WASAPI)
- Plugin implementations now propagate their configuration information back to Roon, to make debug/troubleshooting/certification simpler
- Includes project files for building RAAT on Windows with VS2015

1.0.18 (04/17/2016)
- Added support for standby state and the request_standby method on the source selection plugin

1.0.17 (04/05/2016)
- Fixed bug in software volume that broke forwards compatibility with some 1.2 builds
- Added support for "config_url" in raat_app and RAAT__Info

1.0.16 (03/31/2016)
- Fix some bugs in the script_buffer bindings to enable future performance optimizations
- Support "max_pcm_rate" parameter on ALSA plugin

1.0.15 (03/28/2016)
- For devices with >2 channel input only, zero-pad the remaining channels

1.0.14 (03/09/2016)
- Add output delay to ALSA output plugin

1.0.13 (03/09/2016)
- Add sleep/retries to snd_pcm_hw_params and snd_pcm_prepare to work around bad USB Audio implementation on TEAC-UD501

1.0.12 (02/29/2016)
- Fix typo in performance monitoring interface

1.0.11 (02/16/2016)
- Fix arithmetic overflow when computing time position during ultra-high-resolution playback 

1.0.10 (02/14/2016)
- Wrote a documentation page for raat_app with some sample configurations
- Wait for ALSA devices to become ready with 2s timeout instead of depending on snd_pcm_prepare to succeed immediately
- Add missing S24_LE/S24_BE format support in the 24-bit w/o software volume case, for certain devices

1.0.9 (02/06/2016)

- RAAT supports non-integer volume ranges/values. This is a backwards compatible change
- ALSA volume plugin interface allows volume plugins to communicate more information about dynamic range to Roon
- ALSA volume plugin supports db-based volume controls with non-integer steps.

1.0.8 (02/03/2016)

- ALSA output plugin supports "dop_or_native" and "dcs_or_native" modes for devices that would rather use DoP instead of Native whenever possible

1.0.7 (01/29/2016)

- support for an alsa "watch" plugin, that exits when the device goes away
- fix bug when capturing device info on hardware with multiple ALSA devices

1.0.6 (01/06/2016)

- ALSA Output: support for Native DSD when alsa-lib 1.0.29+ is present

1.0.5 (01/06/2016)

- ALSA Volume: Better auto-searching for mute controls

1.0.4 (01/05/2016)

- ALSA Output: fix crashes when using S24_LE/S24_BE formats
- ALSA Volume: 'index' and 'name' configuration parameters are now optional (see docs for more info)
- Software volume: default attenuation is now -100dB
- RAAT__Info validation rejects empty value for unique_id

1.0.2 (12/29/2015)

- Add support for software-based volume control for PCM streams
- Fixed bad format strings in null and ALSA output plugins
- Fixed bad device ID string when probing ALSA devices for capabilities
- Added <string.h> and <stdio.h> includes to raat_netutil.c 
- Added changelog

1.0.0 (11/07/2015)

- Initial release
